y contains between 2% and 5% of an anti-caking agent—such as corn starch, potato starch or tricalcium phosphate—to  absorb moisture, prevent clumping, and improve flow. Although most often produced in a factory, a proxy for powdered sugar can be made by processing ordinary granulated sugar in a coffee grinder, or by crushing it by hand in a mortar and pestle."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-powdered-sugar"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powdered_sugar"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":13,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Russian tea cake","dish/russian-tea-cake"]]],["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",[["Jésuite","dish/jesuite"]]],["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"]]],["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine",[["Garash cake","dish/garash-cake"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Mille-feuille","dish/mille-feuille"]]],["Galician cuisine","cuisine/galician-cuisine",[["Tarta de Santiago","dish/tarta-de-santiago"]]],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine",[["Stollen","dish/stollen"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Torta della nonna","dish/torta-della-nonna"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Mille-feuille","dish/mille-feuille"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"]]],["Saxon cuisine","cuisine/saxon-cuisine",[["Stollen","dish/stollen"]]],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia",[["Stollen","dish/stollen"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Lard","in